# fixtures/hex/store-f/log.1.hex: extent 1 of store F's log ([F05]), E = 65,536 (spec sync 3, item 9 of
# docs/spec/reviews/spec-sync-3.md). Store F is a small Linux store written as an M9-M10 engine writes it: a
# commit with presence bit 19 and its provenance group, the class-12 `model` symbol, Harvest records (kind 30,
# reserved), BodyDrop records (kind 29) of both origins, and a bulk import whose changeset holds a dropped
# BlobRef. Groups: the epoch-start group; init; f1 and its Harvest records; import/1; the Reserve; the import's
# BodyDrop and f2; the owner's BodyDrop of H1; then the purge's forced rotation pad ([F16] P-101 step 1).
# The pad's trailer is the chain value at lsn 65,536, which log.2's ExtentHead carries as chain_in.
# Bodies (each says it is synthetic):
#   H1 = BLAKE3-128("Synthetic body of note #1 in store F: a made-up token tok-0000-0000 that the owner later drops as a secret.") = d0813361324df4c462dbd76cf3fa29ba
#   H2 = BLAKE3-128("Synthetic body of note #2 in store F: an ordinary paragraph that the owner drops as private after the purge.") = d23f093ec87d06189982bb7e2d7eb71d
#   H3 = BLAKE3-128("Synthetic body of note #3 of store F's import: its exporter had dropped it, so the image carried only its hash.") = fe04735692f1b601490237cfb68a01ed
# The Harvest mark's head is BLAKE3-128 of the 64 stated bytes "synthetic transcript: 64 bytes of made-up text, no owner data...".

